KZ3 patch 2143 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): fixes from the XeSS-SR review, on top of patch 2142. XESSReview.md at the
repository root has the findings (F and M numbers below), the reasoning and the test plan.

- F1: no FXAA on jittered frames. The pass sat between the jitter and the temporal solve.
- F2: the texture mip bias Intel requires, log2(input / target), on the units of jittered scene draws that have a mip
  chain. The jitter decision moves ahead of the sampler table for this. KZ3_XESS_MIP_BIAS overrides it for one run.
- F3: the camera is paired with the renderer frame being built instead of the latest one published, and a dispatch
  checks that it moved on by exactly one flip: the same flip means no camera motion, a skipped flip resets history.
  KZ3_XESS_CAMERA_LAG steps the pairing back; negative restores the old behaviour. "[xess] camera pairing" lines report it.
- F4: a failed draw-time init reports kz3_xess_status() instead of blaming the camera.
- F6: the display surface is captured right after the 3D compose. Pixels the HUD then changed get zero motion and full
  responsiveness, so static text is no longer reprojected with the world. KZ3_XESS_HUD_MASK=0 turns it off for one run.
- F7: a jittered frame that falls back holds jitter off. The next frames still go through XeSS unjittered, and the first
  dispatch that works clears the hold, so Bilinear cannot show a jittering picture for long.
- F10: re-initialising from the present path flushes the open list first. Intel requires pending XeSS work to finish, and
  the waits here only covered submitted lists, so a capture still in the open list could have outlived its texture.
- M2, M3: depth moves into an adapter-owned texture at the scene copy, so no descriptor is rewritten with a frame in
  flight and a later write to the zeta cannot reach XeSS.
- M4: the 250 ms hitch no longer resets history; game time is frame-locked, so a hitch does not invalidate it.
- M8: switching the filter away from XeSS releases the context at the next present.

The rules live in port/kz3/xess_camera.h and xess_inputs.h, with host tests in tools/smoke/test_xess_camera.c and
test_xess_inputs.c. tools/smoke/test_xess.cpp checks the mask and motion contents on a real GPU. Non-KZ3 builds compile
none of this. Written from Intel's public XeSS SDK 3.0.2 developer guide; no game code or Intel source.
